---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { hecklers, stats } from '../data/site';
import officeImg from '../assets/office-chaos.webp';
import profileImg from '../assets/steve-profile.webp';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Steve Martin, The Other One | Wild & Crazy SEO"
  description="A small business SEO consultant who happens to share a name with a famous comedian. No account managers, no contracts, no slide decks. Just the person doing the work."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="hero-eyebrow eyebrow">The Bio · Act One</p>
          <h1>The other<br /><span class="accent">Steve Martin.</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-sub">
            Building websites since 1996, and one lifetime of explaining that no,
            <em>I cannot get you tickets</em>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure class="stage-frame">
          <Image
            src={officeImg}
            alt="Steve Martin in a suit holding floppy disks and a vintage microphone, papers flying, whiteboards covered in growth charts behind him"
            widths={[480, 800, 1200]}
            sizes="(max-width: 940px) 92vw, 520px"
            loading="eager"
          />
          <figcaption>
            My actual tech stack. The floppy disks are for the clients who ask if I back things up.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="bulb-strip" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <section class="playbill">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head" style="max-width:none;">
        <p class="eyebrow">The Long Version</p>
        <h2>How this happened.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose reveal">
        <p>
          I built my first website in 1996. It had a visitor counter, a background tile, and a
          line of text that said "best viewed in Netscape Navigator." It was, at the time,
          genuinely impressive. I have been building them ever since, which means I have
          personally lived through every algorithm update, every redesign trend, and every
          confident prediction that SEO was about to die.
        </p>

        <p>
          I have also had this name the entire time. For the first thirty years it was a
          punchline at the DMV. Then I started doing this for a living and discovered that a
          memorable name is, professionally speaking, an unfair advantage. Nobody forgets who
          did their website.
        </p>

        <p>
          The work itself is not funny at all. Most small businesses are losing customers for
          three or four extremely boring reasons: the site takes nine seconds to load, the
          Google Business Profile has the wrong hours, nobody has published anything since
          2019, and AI assistants have never heard of them. Fix those and the phone rings.
          There is no fifth secret thing. Anyone selling you a fifth secret thing is selling
          you a retainer.
        </p>

        <h3>What working with me actually looks like</h3>

        <p>
          You talk to me. Not a salesperson who disappears after the contract, not an account
          manager who forwards your email to a contractor eleven time zones away. Me. I do the
          audit, I write the plan, I do the work, and when something does not go the way I said
          it would, I am the one who tells you.
        </p>

        <p>
          I take a small number of clients on purpose. It is the only way the above stays true.
          When I am full, I will tell you I am full and point you to somebody good, which is a
          sentence most agencies are physically incapable of saying.
        </p>

        <h3>The name thing</h3>

        <p>
          Yes, I know. No, I have never played the banjo. Yes, someone has sung
          <em>King Tut</em> at me on a discovery call. He is a client now, so I suppose it
          worked.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="playbill" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="stats reveal">
        {
          stats.map((stat) => (
            <div class="stat">
              <div class="num">{stat.num}</div>
              <div class="label">{stat.label}</div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Image
        src={profileImg}
        alt="Steve Martin, SEO consultant, laughing under a spotlight"
        widths={[240, 480]}
        sizes="240px"
        class="headshot"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--text-inverse-muted);">The Short Version</p>
        <h2>Small business SEO, done by one person who answers the phone.</h2>
        <p>
          Local search, AI visibility, technical fixes and websites that load fast. Month to
          month. Plain English. Based wherever the Wi-Fi is, working with businesses that would
          rather be busy than be marketed at.
        </p>
        <div class="credit-line">
          Building websites since 1996 · Zero SNL appearances · One search result at a time
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="playbill">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Hecklers Welcome</p>
        <h2>Questions I get shouted at me.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="heckle-list reveal">
        {
          hecklers.map((item) => (
            <details class="heckle">
              <summary>{item.q}</summary>
              <p class="answer">{item.a}</p>
            </details>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">One Night Only</span>
      <h2>Enough about me.</h2>
      <p>Tell me what your website is doing to you and I will tell you how to stop it.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="ticket-btn">Book Your Free Consult →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
